## Luna subagents

When the operator requests Luna agents, use `$codex-luna-swarm` first; another skill may define
the questions but does not replace it. Resolve every named packet or attachment from the current
message once. If one is absent but the repository and request still define count, authority, and
output, continue and derive the session scopes from the repository. Ask only when the missing material
determines the work. Treat “launch” alone as launch-only; wait and drain only when the
operator also asks to collect, review, or summarise. Say `preparing` until every native call is
accepted or the fallback emits `luna_sessions.started`; only then say `launched`.

Make bounded assumptions and proceed to accepted transport in the same turn. Do not pause for a
plan, task-list, or command approval unless the operator explicitly requested a preview.

Use `max` when no effort is named. Preserve explicit `high`, `xhigh`, or `max`; never silently
upgrade an effort. Native `luna_worker` is fixed to `max`, so use it only for max at 1-15 sessions.
One native catalogue rejection is enough to use the direct launcher for the complete max set.
Use the direct launcher with `--reasoning-effort high` or `xhigh` at every session count. For 16 or
more, use its `--tasks-file` route directly regardless of effort. It has no session-count ceiling.
Resolve that launcher beside the installed repo-scoped Skill; never use a global or copied
launcher. Give every session one distinct owned angle, starting point, authority, and outcome. Keep
common evidence in one packet, require hypotheses only for causal or defect questions, and validate
meaning rather than exact phrases. Let read-only sessions propose fixes; implement only in the main
session after verification unless write sessions have isolated ownership. Use `--launch-only` for
start-only work; omit it for collection and verify the host loads the Stop hook before relying on it. Preserve
Luna identity and never substitute Sol, Terra, or a coordinator. Do not read or reimplement the
launcher.
<!-- codex-luna-swarm:end -->
